# short-description: Ultima gauge cluster image (falcon boot): SD boot + root + ext4 /data
# long-description: Three partitions on the SD card (this board has no eMMC):
#   p1  vfat "boot"  tiboot3.bin (falcon-configured R5 SPL) + tifalcon.bin
#                    (ATF + OP-TEE + DM + kernel Image + DTB in one FIT) —
#                    that is the whole boot chain: R5 SPL -> ATF -> OP-TEE ->
#                    kernel. No A53 SPL, no U-Boot proper, no GRUB, no
#                    separate Image/dtb/grub.cfg on the card. The kernel
#                    cmdline lives in the DTB inside tifalcon.bin (see
#                    recipes-bsp/ultima-falcon-fit).
#   p2  ext4 "root"  rootfs, mounted read-only (--no-fstab-update: the stock
#                    fstab's `/dev/root / auto ro` is what we want)
#   p3  ext4 "data"  the only persistent writable partition (odometer etc.),
#                    mounted by ultima-data-mount
#
# History: until 2026-08-30 this used a bootimg-efi layout (GRUB via U-Boot's
# EFI loader, `dtb=` sourceparam and `console=ttyS2,115200n8 earlycon` on the
# bootloader line were the two fixes that got this board's display working —
# see the BeagleY-AI notes "display works end to end"). Falcon
# makes all of that moot: the
# DTB is chosen and the cmdline set at build time in the FIT, so the wks has
# nothing bootloader-related left to say. The stock (GRUB) chain from a
# pre-falcon build remains the fallback on the bench — see NOTES.md "Falcon
# on BeagleY-AI" for the file swap — but a falcon build's own tispl.bin no
# longer works (its bl31 jumps to 0x82000000, where the kernel goes, not to
# the A53 SPL), which is why it isn't on the card at all.
#
# IMAGE_BOOT_FILES (tiboot3.bin tifalcon.bin) is set in this layer's
# tisdk-base-image.bbappend, next to the do_image_wic dependency on
# ultima-falcon-fit that makes tifalcon.bin exist before wic runs.
# resize_rootfs.service stays masked in that bbappend (root is read-only).
part --source bootimg-partition --fstype=vfat --label boot --active --align 1024 --use-uuid --fixed-size 128M
part / --source rootfs --fstype=ext4 --label root --align 1024 --use-uuid --no-fstab-update
part /data --fstype=ext4 --label data --fixed-size 16M --align 1024
